WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.450
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.408
SPEAKER: In a world where
virtual collaboration

00:00:02.408 --> 00:00:05.250
and digital transformation
is increasingly important

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:08.520
for organizations, finding
better ways that your team can

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.920
leverage technology to
work more efficiently

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.170
is critical to success.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.990
This is especially true
for desk-less workers,

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.000
who are out on the
floor or in the field

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.770
and not at a computer.

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:22.650
For these people, it can be
challenging to create solutions

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.930
that address their needs.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.390
Luckily, Google Cloud
is here to help.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:29.670
We'll show how a team
of field technicians

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.040
can leverage Google
Cloud products to boost

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:33.660
their productivity.

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:35.100
In just a few
minutes, you should

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.320
be able to walk away with
some new ideas of how

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.450
you can harness the
power of technology

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:42.780
to improve the way you
and your team works.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.040
Meet Julia.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.860
Julia manages a team of
appliance repair experts

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:50.610
who respond to dozens of
job requests each day.

00:00:50.610 --> 00:00:53.840
Julia needs an easy way to
communicate with her team,

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:56.100
manage the job
requests and contracts,

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.020
and provide her team
with the resources they

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.220
need to do their job.

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:01.890
So how does she do it?

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:04.410
Well, in just a
couple days, Julia

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.920
has used App Sheet, Google
Cloud's no code application

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.250
development platform, to
create a simple app to help

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:13.410
her manage all these tasks.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:14.940
She shared this
app with her team

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.550
so they can all
collaborate around it.

00:01:17.550 --> 00:01:19.590
The first task Julia
needs to complete

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:22.380
is to be able to
communicate with her team.

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:25.410
Julia has set up a virtual
daily standup for her team

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:28.230
that can be joined by
selecting Daily Standup,

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.540
then clicking on Today's Event.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.640
This opens up a Google Meet.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.000
Julia can then discuss over
video chat the key items,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.460
and each member of her
team can share their plan

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.740
for the action of the day.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:44.220
Customers fill out new job
requests through Google Forms,

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.320
and as the requests
come in, they

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:49.710
will show up in the Jobs
section of Julia's app.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.092
She can then assign them to
the different technicians,

00:01:52.092 --> 00:01:53.550
and they can work
with the customer

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:57.660
to schedule and
complete the repair.

00:01:57.660 --> 00:01:59.610
When a technician
picks up a job,

00:01:59.610 --> 00:02:03.450
they're able to easily create
a job contract in the app.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:12.050
They simply fill out
some key information,

00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:17.000
sign it, and save it.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.800
The app then
automatically updates

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.870
a template that was
created in Google

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:23.450
Docs with the
appropriate information

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:26.060
and sends it to Julia
and the customer.

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:29.060
This app links directly
to a Google Sheet,

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:33.050
so anytime Julia or her team
makes updates to the app,

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:36.080
the sheet is updated
with the new information.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:38.990
This makes it easy for
Julia to manage her data

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:42.090
and know where
everything is stored.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:44.160
As the technician
works on a repair,

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.380
they're able to access
the manuals and repair

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:48.780
guides associated with
that product, which

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:52.200
have been uploaded to the
drive and linked in the app.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.170
This makes it easy for her team
to access the documentation

00:02:55.170 --> 00:02:57.930
they need while on the job.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.780
Finally, as a technician
completes a job,

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:09.960
they're able to update its
status with details, pictures,

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.270
and even annotations.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:17.270
These types of apps aren't just
useful for appliance repair

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:18.140
teams.

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:21.340
They can be used by construction
workers, inspectors,

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:24.380
health care workers, public
service representatives,

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:25.700
and more.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.680
Using these Google
Cloud platforms,

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.600
creating processes
such as these can

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.330
take days or weeks,
not months or years,

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:37.220
to create, allowing businesses
to work faster and better.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.480
To learn more and to access
this and other app templates,

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:41.480
click on the link below.

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:44.230
[MUSIC PLAYING]

